{
  "schema_version": "loquitur.public_api_parity.v1",
  "description": "The public APIs of the two reference verifiers, loquitur-verify-py and loquitur-verify-ts, side by side: every export, every member of a result an export returns and every report member that carries a verdict, a status, an authorization, a signature, a root or a trust result, with its counterpart in the other verifier or none and the reason. The same file is tools/public_api_parity.json in loquitur-verify-py and scripts/public-api-parity.json in loquitur-verify-ts; each repository's tests hold it to that repository's exports, and to the sibling's copy when the sibling is checked out. The differential harness of loquitur-conformance (tools/differential) calls the operations named in ops through each verifier's test-only adapter and compares the answers.",
  "naming": {
    "py": "loquitur.verify.NAME is a name of loquitur.verify.__all__; loquitur.verify.MODULE.NAME[.MEMBER] a name of a module of the package, reached by import, and MEMBER a field or property of a result class; report:PATH a member of the report verify_path returns, as to_dict writes it",
    "ts": "NAME is a name src/index.ts or src/index.browser.ts exports, a value or a type; TYPE.MEMBER[.MEMBER] a member of an exported type, and VerifyReport.checks.NAME a per-check result a run writes; internal:FILE#NAME a function a module of src/ exports and neither entry does"
  },
